BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Throwback Thursdays: Great Movies on the Big Screen
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T200000
UID:6ad7caf5a85a2c003380dcff@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Come join us for a radical retro rewind projected on the big s
 creen. Whether you're a first-time viewer or long-time fan\, these movies 
 are sure to please.\nOctober 22: Aliens (1986\, 14+)\nOctober 29: Scream 
 (1996\, 18A)\nNovember 5: Knives Out: Glass Onion (2022\, PG)\nNovember 1
 2: Hitch (2005\, PG-13)\nNovember 19: Forrest Gump (1994\, PG)\nNovember 2
 6: The Shawshank Redemption (1994\, 14A)\nAll are welcome. Drop-in\, no r
 egistration required.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad7caf5a85a2c003380dcff
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coding with Python
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T160000
UID:6ac6488129c3d600332e3b5c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This is a 2-part series\, participants are expected to attend 
 both sessions.\nPython is an open source programming language that is used
  for creating web applications\, web content\, mathematics and system scri
 pting. In this course you will learn how python code works and given time 
 to practice. Prior coding knowledge is not necessary for this introductory
  class\, but you should be confident with using a computer. Key takeaways
  will include a working knowledge of variables\, loops\, conditional argum
 ents and more.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information o
 n this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Li
 braries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will onl
 y be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Qu
 estions about how the library handles your information can be directed to 
 Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street
 \, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Forest Hill\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac6488129c3d600332e3b5c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
