BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What is the Universe Made of?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T150000
UID:6ad24e72e06996003a83ed3e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:You can see so much around you\, buildings\, trees\, clouds\, 
 rain\, and more. But is that what the universe is really made of? When we 
 study the universe\, we get a much different answer.\nLearn about how scie
 ntists detected the presence of invisible “dark matter” and what that 
 revealed about our universe\, and how we are studying it today!\nDrop-in\,
  no registration required!
LOCATION:Wychwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad24e72e06996003a83ed3e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
