BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Tie-Dye
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T190000
UID:6ac681aa2b40e729fed1acab@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in the Youth Hub for some tie-dying! Choose from a t-s
 hirt\, or a TPL tote bag\, and you can even bring in your own white cotton
  garments to dye as well! Participants will take home their freshly tie-d
 yed creations on the same day\; be prepared to rinse\, wash\, and dry you
 r creations once you arrive home so that your project comes out its best. 
 We also recommend wearing old clothes so that you don't get any dyes on yo
 ur favourite outfit!\nTie Dye Aftercare Instructions:\n- Let the dye sit f
 or 6-8 hours\, or up to 24 hours for a more vibrant look.\n- Remove the el
 astics\, and rinse out our item until the water runs clear. It will take l
 onger than you think! (Tip: put your item in the shower and use the shower
  head to rinse it out).\n- Wash your item with detergent.\n- Dry your item
 .\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming p
 lace for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are al
 ways available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a br
 anch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Maria A. Shchuka\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac681aa2b40e729fed1acab
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
