BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Coding with Python II
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T200000
UID:6ac55e37377296003a4a28ac@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Python is an open source programming language that is used for
  creating web applications\, web content\, mathematics and system scriptin
 g. In this second Python session we will leverage everything we learned a
 bout loops and blocks in part one to create our very own functions. We'll 
 take a look at how to approach function design\, how to allow users to ent
 er data into functions through arguments\, and how to get our functions to
  return results. We will also introduce some new data structures which\, u
 nlike variables\, can hold more than one piece of data at a time.\nThis cl
 ass is for beginners but assumes you have a basic understanding of Python 
 or have attended Coding with Python I.\nRegistration will start 2 weeks be
 fore this class. Computers will be provided.\nInformation Collection Notic
 e:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publ
 ic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 2
 0(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration
 \, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your i
 nformation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 4
 16-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Cliffcrest\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ac55e37377296003a4a28ac
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Set Phasers to Celebrate! 60 Years of Star Trek: A Merril Collecti
 on Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260817T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261101T235959
UID:6a4d01876bd493f6008f06ce@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Beam yourself up to the Merril Collection of Science Fiction\,
  Speculation and Fantasy and boldly embark on a 60-year journey that cele
 brates all things Star Trek! For decades\, the original television serie
 s turned global franchise has inspired generations of fans\, artists\, and
  scientists alike. Visitors can explore voyages\, characters\, and new f
 rontiers through our collection highlights such as novels\, RPGs\, fanzine
 s\, original artwork and more!\nThis exhibit can be viewed during the Merr
 il Collection's regular open hours.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Merril Collection Reading Room\, 3rd Floor. Ex
 hibit is open during the same hours as the branch.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4d01876bd493f6008f06ce
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Photo Editing with Photoshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261126T200000
UID:6abbe8cde06996003a800482@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Adobe Photoshop is the world’s best imaging and graphic desi
 gn software and is at the core of just about every creative project\, from
  photo editing and compositing to digital painting\, animation\, and graph
 ic design.\nJoin us for an introductory lesson and learn about the most co
 mmon tools. We'll explore the workspace and enhance images while investiga
 ting tools such as crop\, levels\, colour balance and more. See how an ima
 ge can be altered and repaired using patch tools such as the clone and hea
 ling brush tools. We'll also dive deep into the world of layers and how yo
 u can manage them for those really unique and fun projects.\nRegistration 
 is required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Davenport\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abbe8cde06996003a800482
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
