BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Learning Things You Love with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T180000
UID:6a9c345929a7dd0d67493d38@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Always wanted to learn to cook\, draw\, knit\, fix a bike\, or
  speak another language\, but have trouble sticking to it? What if you had
  a personal AI tutor?\nIn this class with our Innovator-in-Residence\,\nRy
 an Kelln\n\, learn how AI can become your personal tutor for something you
  love\, or something new you want to fall in love with. A tutor explains t
 hings in the way you understand\, asks you questions\, and helps you choos
 e what to learn next. Learn how to turn your goal into a specific\, doable
  learning experiment: options not answers\, with a practice that survives 
 a bad day. Decide ahead of time how you'll know it's working: revise\, or 
 stop without guilt. You'll leave with a plan you actually want to try\, an
 d a sense for what AI should never decide for you.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\
 , keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding exp
 erience required.\nRegistration is required and will start October 9\, 202
 6 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of 
 the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be fille
 d on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nIf you w
 ish to save your work from this hands-on program\, please bring your own U
 SB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includes 
 activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.\nY
 ou do not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipants 
 are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\, w
 hich include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review the p
 rivacy statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude Co
 de\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn
  more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Antigravity\nLearn mor
 e about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more abou
 t the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe per
 sonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library 
 under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The i
 nformation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery
  and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information 
 can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981
 \, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c345929a7dd0d67493d38
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
