DESCRIPTION:A fast-paced\, fun session where young creators tackle a real 
 community challenge through brainstorming\, sketching\, and creative think
 ing. There are no wrong answers\, just ideas\, energy\, and collaboration.
  If time allows\, you might even start building a simple version of your s
 olution.\nArrive 30 minutes before or stay 30 minutes after the program fo
 r one-on-one consultations.\nThis program is part of TPL's Innovator in Re
 sidence series focused on civic innovation. From October 5 to November 28\
 , join programs\, workshops and one-on-one consultations led by technology
  strategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help you create pos
 itive change in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\nInformation 
 Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
 ram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the librar
 y handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerl
 ine@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Second floor\, Digitial Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe885e295b3b0033ca3742
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
