BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Innovating Civic History
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T200000
UID:6abe89da11bbf300684aa7ff@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:We dig into a real civic issue from the past\, one that was ei
 ther solved\, stalled\, or never fully addressed and ask: what would we do
  differently today? Using modern tools\, fresh perspectives\, and communit
 y knowledge\, participants analyze what happened and propose new approache
 s. History is the starting point\; innovation is the goal.\nArrive 30 minu
 tes before or stay 30 minutes after the program for one-on-one consultatio
 ns.\nThis program is part of TPL's Innovator in Residence series focused o
 n civic innovation. From October 5 to November 28\, join programs\, worksh
 ops and one-on-one consultations led by technology strategist Ismail Moham
 ud to learn how technology can help you create positive change in your com
 munity. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe 
 personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libra
 ry under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). Th
 e information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliv
 ery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informati
 on can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Second Floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abe89da11bbf300684aa7ff
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
