BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Video Editing with Da Vinci Resolve Parts I and II
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T200000
UID:6abbe5329abb62002c6af83f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This two part introductory series will cover the layout\, t
 ools and workflow used for video editing in DaVinci Resolve. Part I\, whi
 ch will take place on\nNovember 10th\n\, will cover basic video editing t
 echniques such as inserting and trimming media\, transitions\, titles\, ad
 ding audio\, and using flags and markers.\nPart II will be held on\nNovemb
 er 17th\n\, where participants will become familiar with some of the more 
 advanced tools in DaVinci’s Editing page such as key framing transform e
 ffects\, cropping\, adjusting clip speed\, normalizing audio\, and simple 
 compositing.\nComputers will be provided for this program.\nInformation Co
 llection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by th
 e Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\,
  20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and progra
 m registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library 
 handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerlin
 e@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Davenport\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abbe5329abb62002c6af83f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Time Capsule: VHS & Film Negatives
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261103T193000
UID:6ae23c8d901b02002cc5c351@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Preserve your favourite memories for the future! In this hands
 -on session\, staff will show you how to digitize VHS tapes and photo nega
 tives using the equipment in the Digital Innovation Hub. Learn how to conv
 ert your old media into modern digital files that you can store\, share\, 
 and enjoy for years to come.\nAll equipment is provided. Please bring your
  own VHS tapes or film negatives to convert.\nNo computer experience requi
 red\nAll Ages Welcome!!
LOCATION:Downsview
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ae23c8d901b02002cc5c351
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Buying a Car? Know Your Rights!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T150000
UID:6ab2c187ab7a8e0037c39dc2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Buying a vehicle can be a challenging experience with long-ter
 m financial implications.\nJoin us for an in-person presentation by the\nO
 ntario Motor Vehicle Industry Council (OMVIC)\n\, the regulator of motor v
 ehicle sales in Ontario. A representative from OMVIC will provide you with
  resources and tips for buying new and used cars in Ontario.\nTopics will 
 include:\nOMVIC’s Compensation Fund\nUnderstanding Car Dealer Advertisin
 g\nNegative Equity & Long Term Loans\nAgreement & Disclosure\nAvoiding Cur
 bsides & Fraud Prevention\nTips for Buying or Leasing a Car\nAges 16-up & 
 drop-in\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this 
 form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries
  Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be us
 ed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions
  about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerl
 ine staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto
  ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bendale\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab2c187ab7a8e0037c39dc2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
