BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Recharge your Mind: A Social Wellness Event for Teens and Parents
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261107T160000
UID:6ab6d9b108693b0f7374a4af@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a fun and supportive day designed to boost social 
 wellness and connection! Teens can explore engaging workshops and activiti
 es\, including mental skills preparation\, art journaling\, and creative c
 rafts— meet other teens\, and take a relaxing break with therapy dogs.\n
 Parents/Caregivers are invited to a dedicated workshop delivered by regist
 ered psychotherapist Ola Obaro. Gain practical strategies for setting bo
 undaries\, managing conflict\, and strengthening relationships with your t
 een while letting go of parenting guilt.\nEnjoy refreshments\, receive a g
 oody bag\, and take part in activities that encourage creativity\, connect
 ion\, and self-expression.\nThis is a free event —\nregister to secure y
 our spot!\nRegister the total number of attendees\, including adults and t
 eens. Walk-ins are welcome if there’s space available.\nGot questions a
 bout the event? Please email us at teens@tpl.ca\nThis event is part of TPL
 's Teen Social Health and Wellness programming.\nGenerously supported by:\
 nThe Estate of Claudia Krawchuk
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Second floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6d9b108693b0f7374a4af
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
