  Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261123T190000
UID:6aaa95e465abe8002a79a77f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Expand your connections and opportunities with our Networking 
 Workshop for Youth Entrepreneurs! You will learn how to build meaningful p
 rofessional relationships\, communicate confidently\, and leverage their n
 etworks for business growth. Through interactive activities and expert tip
 s\, you will gain the skills to connect with mentors\, partners\, and pote
 ntial customers.\nRegistration required. Limited spots. Young Adults (ages
  18-24) have priority for this workshop.\nThis program will be taking plac
 e in\nLearning Centre 2\n\,\nlocated on the first floor (next to the book 
 store and TD Gallery).\n----\nThis workshop is part of the Youth for Entre
 preneurship program led by the YMCA of Greater Toronto. Through hands-on s
 essions\, you’ll gain the digital tools\, financial knowledge\, and crea
 tive strategies needed to build a business idea from the ground up.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Learning Centre 2 (1st floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaa95e465abe8002a79a77f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
