BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Learning Things You Love with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T200000
UID:6a9c35d7be148200298cb292@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Always wanted to learn to cook\, draw\, knit\, fix a bike\, or
  speak another language\, but have trouble sticking to it? What if you had
  a personal AI tutor?\nIn this class led by our Innovator-in-Residence\,\n
 Ryan Kelln\n\, learn how AI can become your personal tutor for something y
 ou love\, or something new you want to fall in love with. A tutor explains
  things in the way you understand\, asks you questions\, and helps you cho
 ose what to learn next. Learn how to turn your goal into a specific\, doab
 le learning experiment: options not answers\, with a practice that survive
 s a bad day. Decide ahead of time how you'll know it's working: revise\, o
 r stop without guilt. You'll leave with a plan you actually want to try\, 
 and a sense for what AI should never decide for you.\nPrerequisites: Mous
 e\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are provided. No coding e
 xperience required.\nRegistration is required and will start November 9\, 
 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes 
 of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining seats will be fi
 lled on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is reached.\nIf yo
 u wish to save your work from this hands-on program\, please bring your ow
 n USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis program includ
 es activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on library laptops.
 \nYou do not need to create your own account for this program.\nParticipan
 ts are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throughout sessions\
 , which include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage you to review th
 e privacy statements of each tool prior to attending this program:\nClaude
  Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nClaude Cowork\nLe
 arn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Antigravity\nLearn 
 more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studio\nLearn more a
 bout the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe 
 personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libra
 ry under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). Th
 e information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliv
 ery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informati
 on can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5
 981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c35d7be148200298cb292
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
