BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Democracy Fitness - Disagreement
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T170000
UID:6ad8f63b2b40e729fed332cd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Develop and exercise the skills you need to be an active parti
 cipant in everyday democracy in this fun\, interactive session. Democracy 
 Fitness expands traditional ideas of what democracy is by exploring how pe
 ople participate in civic life\, build understanding and work together.\nI
 n this session\, we’ll exercise our Disagreement muscles. In a democracy
 \, disagreement is natural\, but it can feel uncomfortable. If you can sta
 y disagreed\, you gain knowledge and respect. Through a 30-min series of s
 hort\, interactive exercises\, you'll explore where your opinions fall on 
 a variety of topics\, practice staying in disagreement\, and strengthen yo
 ur ability to engage in constructive dialogue across differences.\nGenerou
 sly supported by: McConnell Foundation\nRegister with staff in the Youth H
 ub beginning\nNovember 1\nst\n. Drop-ins are welcome.\nThis program is par
 t of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after s
 chool and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\
 , nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub
 \nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Albion\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad8f63b2b40e729fed332cd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Democracy Fitness - Verbal Confidence
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261124T170000
UID:6ad8f6ce11bbf300684cd2ab@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Develop and exercise the skills you need to be an active parti
 cipant in everyday democracy in this fun\, interactive session. Democracy 
 Fitness expands traditional ideas of what democracy is by exploring how pe
 ople participate in civic life\, build understanding and work together.\nI
 n this session\, we’ll exercise our Verbal Confidence muscles. In a demo
 cracy\, we all have a voice. If your voice is warm and you know what to sa
 y\, your words can make an impact. Through a 30-min series of short\, inte
 ractive exercises\, you'll get familiar with your voice\, think about your
  perspective on different issues\, and practice speaking out about a cause
  that matters to you. This workshop will strengthen your ability to partic
 ipate in civic life.\nGenerously supported by: McConnell Foundation\nRegis
 tration is required. Register with staff in the Youth Hub beginning\nNovem
 ber 1\nst\n. Drop-ins are welcome.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub serv
 ice. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the su
 mmer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks
  are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branc
 h to find out more.
LOCATION:Albion\, Auditorium
