BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Democracy Fitness - Compromise
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T170000
UID:6ad8f79711bbf300684cd2df@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Develop and exercise the skills you need to be an active parti
 cipant in everyday democracy in this fun\, interactive session. Democracy 
 Fitness expands traditional ideas of what democracy is by exploring how pe
 ople participate in civic life\, build understanding and work together.\nI
 n this session\, we’ll exercise our Compromise muscles. In a democracy\,
  we find solutions together. When we make room for each other's approaches
 \, more people can accept the decisions. Through a 30-min series of short\
 , interactive exercises\, you'll find out how you prefer to make decisions
 \, practice solving a problem with those who think like you\, and practice
  compromising with those who might think differently. This workshop will s
 trengthen your ability to engage in meaningful dialogue.\nGenerously suppo
 rted by: McConnell Foundation\nRegistration is required. Register with sta
 ff in the Youth Hub beginning\nNovember 1st.\nDrop-ins are welcome.\nThis 
 program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for
  teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always ava
 ilable. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch wit
 h a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Albion\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad8f79711bbf300684cd2df
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Hands-On Dinosaur Fossils & Ancient Life
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261117T173000
UID:6ad8feecebad22004546ee39@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an opportunity to handle\, examine up close and di
 scuss nine real and replica fossils in this fascinating hands-on workshop.
  Participants will be entertained and educated\, not just about the fossil
 s themselves\, but the palaeontological aspects that underpin them. Concep
 ts include: evolution\, fossilization\, ‘The Tree of Life’ (phylogeny)
  and — of course — dinosaurs!\nAll teens are welcome! Drop-in\, no reg
 istration required.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs
  are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer\, where he
 lpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered da
 ily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out m
 ore.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Youth Hub (on the second floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad8feecebad22004546ee39
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
