DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261118T173000
UID:6ad90057a85a2c0033811b36@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​Learn hands-on about every creative stage involved in makin
 g a mini-comic\, starting from an idea\, character designing\, script writ
 ing\, rough sketching a comic page\, and inking\, then making copies to tr
 ade your finished comic with friends!\nThis workshop will be led by comics
  artist and writer\, Jason Loo (Marvel Comics\; The Pitiful Human Lizard).
 \nAll teens are welcome! Drop-in\, no registration required.\nThis program
  is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens 
 after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always available.
  Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYo
 uth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
