BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Mindfulness Through Art
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T190000
UID:6ad900f0ad402765915493e5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Mindfulness Through Art\nis a fun\, creative workshop where yo
 u'll explore simple mindfulness tools that can help with stress\, anxiety\
 , and feeling overwhelmed. Create your own Mindfulness Jar to see what the
  mind can feel like when thoughts are racing and learn easy breathing and 
 grounding techniques that can help bring a sense of calm and focus. You'll
  also take part in a colouring activity that helps you identify where emot
 ions show up in your body and discover how mindfulness can help you feel m
 ore present\, balanced\, and connected. No art skills or mindfulness exper
 ience needed\, just come ready to relax\, create\, and try something new!\
 nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming pla
 ce for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are alwa
 ys available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a bran
 ch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Parkdale\, Basement
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad900f0ad402765915493e5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
