DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T173000
UID:6ada6230ebad22004547398e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This henna art program will offer participants the opportunity
  to create their own unique henna designs. Through guided instruction\, pa
 rticipants learn about the history and cultural significance of henna\, as
  well as techniques for creating intricate patterns. Participants are enco
 uraged to explore their creativity and design their own patterns\, which t
 hey then apply using henna paste. Through hands-on experience\, participan
 ts can express themselves artistically while learning a traditional art fo
 rm.\nInformation Collection Notice: The personal information on this form 
 is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\
 , sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used fo
 r event and program registration\, delivery\, and evaluation. Questions ab
 out how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline
  staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON
  M4W 2G8.
