DESCRIPTION:Ever wonder why stretching feels so good\, or why one deep bre
 ath can change your whole mood?\nWellness Unplugged is a laid-back worksho
 p where teens can dig into the science and history behind yoga and Pilates
 . No experience\, no equipment\, no pressure. Come ready for honest conver
 sations\, journaling\, and hands-on activities that give you real tools fo
 r everyday life.\nHosted by the Villij\, a Toronto-based wellness company 
 rooted in mindful movement and community connection. Drop in. No registrat
 ion required.\nThis workshop is part of the Teen Social Health and Wellnes
 s programming. Generously supported by The Estate of Claudia Krawchuk.\nTh
 is program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place 
 for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always 
 available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch 
 with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Kennedy/Eglinton
