  to both sessions\n(November 14 and 28) and optionally\, your own time de
 signing a book cover and/or foredge stencils.\nNovember 14 2-4:30pm\n- Pa
 rt 1 Preparing the book\, customize the book (end papers\, book ribbon\, 
 headbands)\, making the hard case\nOptional at home:\nDesign cover vinyl 
 or edge stencil.\nNovember 28 2-4:30pm\n- Part 2 Adding the vinyl (optiona
 l if you have designed a cover)\, painting the edges (optional)\, puttin
 g the book together\nPick up 1 week later\nRegistration is required.\nThis
  program is intended for teens and young adults only.\nLate entrants past 
 10 minutes will not be admitted.\nInformation Collection Notice: The perso
 nal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library un
 der the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inf
 ormation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery a
 nd evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 78
 9 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Room BC
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ad28fed035faf0033dd2504
