BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Data Exploration and Introduction to AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T200000
UID:6abc20d211bbf300684a75f2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:There is more information about your world than you might thin
 k\, and the tools to make sense of it are more accessible than ever. This 
 session introduces public data sources like the Toronto Open Data Portal a
 nd Kaggle\, then shows you how AI tools can help you explore and analyze t
 hat data without any technical background. You will learn how to find data
 sets relevant to a civic issue\, ask AI the right questions to surface ins
 ights\, and turn raw numbers into something meaningful. No experience requ
 ired.\nArrive 30 minutes before or stay 30 minutes after the program for o
 ne-on-one consultations.\nThis program is part of TPL's Innovator in Resid
 ence series focused on civic innovation. From October 5 to November 28\, j
 oin programs\, workshops and one-on-one consultations led by technology st
 rategist Ismail Mohamud to learn how technology can help you create positi
 ve change in your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\nInformation Col
 lection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the
  Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 
 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program
  registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library h
 andles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline
 @tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Second floor\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc20d211bbf300684a75f2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
