BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Improv For Wellness Program
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261120T170000
UID:6ace5b3e96ec3a003ada461e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Laughter is good for the soul! Improv is an opportunity to exp
 lore the value of presence\, acceptance\, collaboration and a sense of hum
 our. Join special presenter Ashley Seaman as she leads participants thr
 ough creative exercises and games to connect\, create and laugh! Want to g
 et ready for a presentation at school? Prep your acting skills for an audi
 tion? Or want to more confident in general? Feel free to come drop-in for
  our Improv session program!\nDrop-in until capacity is reached\nThis prog
 ram is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for tee
 ns after school and in the summer\, where helpful staff are always availab
 le. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\
 nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
 Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, a
 nd 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registra
 tion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n
 \, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ace5b3e96ec3a003ada461e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Edible Slime Making
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261104T170000
UID:6ababd589dbc2b002c8ad258@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us in the Youth Hub to make edible slime! Using your sens
 es\, get creative\, and learn about mindfulness while crafting a delicious
  treat to take home.\nAll materials provided. Please register to reserve y
 our spot. 15 participants max.\nFood allergy notice: Please be aware that 
 food will be used in this program.  Certain food ingredients may cause all
 ergic reactions in some people.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service
 . Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summe
 r\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks ar
 e offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch t
 o find out more.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ababd589dbc2b002c8ad258
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Ukelele for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261106T163000
UID:6abaed879dbc2b002c8ae74e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have fun learning a new instrument - the ukulele! This worksho
 p will cover fundamentals of ukulele playing. By the end of this class\, y
 ou'll be able to start playing your first songs on the ukulele! Beginner f
 riendly\, no previous experience is necessary.\nThis program is part of Yo
 uth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school a
 nd in the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutri
 tious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor ca
 ll the branch to find out more.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe perso
 nal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library un
 der the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inf
 ormation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery a
 nd evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information ca
 n be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\,
  789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abaed879dbc2b002c8ae74e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Novel Writing Challenge
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261105T173000
UID:6abaefed9dbc2b002c8ae812@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:It doesn’t matter if the writing is good - what matters is t
 hat it’s out on the page. Join us for speed novel writing as a group wit
 h challenges and support from others to get those words from your head to 
 the page!\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a wel
 coming place for teens after school and in the summer\, where helpful staf
 f are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offered daily. Drop
  by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Youth Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abaefed9dbc2b002c8ae812
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Spoken Word Workshop - Rhythm and Poetry
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261113T183000
UID:6abc07480f56a0002cd4d0bd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this program led by spoken word coach Joshua Watkis\, parti
 cipants will learn the history and mechanics of Rhythm and Poetry (Rap)\, 
 practice basic rhyme schemes and literary devices\, and write and share th
 eir own 8-16 bar verse.\nThis program is part of Youth Hub service. Youth 
 Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school and in the summer\, wher
 e helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutritious snacks are offere
 d daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor call the branch to find o
 ut more.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc07480f56a0002cd4d0bd
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wellness Connections: Workshops for Mental Health & Emotional Well
 ness Part 2
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261127T153000
UID:6abc3851de300e0045171492@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a series of group workshops for anyone interested 
 in strengthening their mental well-being\, understanding their emotions an
 d developing practical strategies for coping with life’s challenges.\nPa
 rt 2: Building Resilience (\n4 weeks\, Every Friday\, 2-3:30 pm\, Nov 27 -
  Dec 18\, 2026)\nRecognise your strengths and develop personalised strateg
 ies for navigating challenges\, building resilience and maintaining mental
  wellness.\nTTC Presto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks and refreshments 
 are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at
  the program.\nRegistration is required.\nAttend all 4 sessions to receive
  a certificate.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nCanadian Mental He
 alth Association Toronto\n.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal 
 information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under 
 the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informa
 tion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and e
 valuation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be
  directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789
  Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3 (2nd floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6abc3851de300e0045171492
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
